From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:03:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] softisp: preserve sensor-space LSC mapping and gain range

Adapt the preceding Mei Tao LSC-statistics patch to preserve sensor-
space calibration geometry and all supported Lenovo mesh gains on
upstream v0.8.0.

Resample full-reference uniform tables for the actual analogue crop,
after subtracting the active-area origin. Other IPA engines keep their
hardware-node table interpretation unless they explicitly request
resampling. Keep fractional register-domain data until crop
interpolation, then round and validate rather than silently truncate or
overflow. Reset the colour-temperature cache when the mode changes and
populate the first frame even when its initial temperature is zero.

Map normalized sensor coordinates to the centres of the 17x17 texture
nodes. Correct unpacked Bayer stride padding independently of the
optical calibration field. Use the same node mapping and profile scale
for statistics, rebuilding the cached gains when the scale changes even
if the table version does not. Clamp below-black noise to the preserved
pedestal before applying gains, matching the renderer's nonnegative
signal rather than reducing the IPA's averaged brightness with amplified
negative samples. Preserve CPU/no-LSC statistics.

Default existing profiles to the original RGBA8 scale of four. Allow an
explicit validated scale for tabular profiles only, and carry it in the
per-frame debayer parameters and shader uniforms. The ThinkSmart profile
uses scale 255/59: byte 59 is unity, and 59 is the largest integral
unity code that preserves the vendor maximum of 4.30724 without
clipping. This minimizes quantization while retaining RGBA8
compatibility. The mesh is still not a lossless floating-point
calibration. Gate LSC in the shader using the actual per-frame enable
control; disabling it must not accidentally apply the new encoding to
the legacy identity table. Warn explicitly if a CPU fallback cannot
apply the configured LSC.

Exercise the actual sensor crop rectangles, asymmetric
interpolation/orientation, rejected out-of-reference crops, exact unity,
black-pedestal and saturation handling, and enabled/disabled/CPU-
fallback statistics. Include the same-version gain-scale transition in
the focused Android/Meson regression target. The Android regression and
AGC frame-duration regression pass on ThinkSmart. A sensor-free GLES2
render check of the actual packed/unpacked RAW10/RAW12 shaders passes on
both Mesa llvmpipe and the ThinkSmart Adreno 506 (FD506), checking
padded stride, node mapping, disable, unity and above-four gains within
two 8-bit output codes. These exercise the implementation, including the
device GPU, but not camera-buffer/request integration, physical lens
flat-field correction or factory-equivalent image quality.

Base-commit: df8e348d64b4932a0676256ed24f0da3ee9438bc
Source: https://github.com/rickx/ubuntu-thinksmart/blob/6f5b14928a873d171e1deddb5edbdc6967c86aa2/sources/patches/libcamera/0002-libcamera-software_isp-Apply-LSC-gains-to-the-sta.patch
